family: web-ui
what: poll
transport: v2c
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: reference
reference: RFC 3416 (SNMP operations), RFC 3414 (SNMPv3 users)
does: The values to enter in the device's SNMP agent page so Woodshed can poll it (SNMPv2c, read-only).
check: Devices → Add polling → Test poll answers with the device's name and interfaces.
placeholders: <COMMUNITY>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- Then add the device in Woodshed: Devices → Add polling, its address, SNMPv2c and the same community.
- Field names differ between devices; some also need SNMP allowed on the interface Woodshed reaches.
---- part steps "": In the device's web page, open its SNMP agent settings and enter
SNMP agent: on
SNMP version: v2c
Read-only community: <COMMUNITY>
Allowed managers (if asked): 192.0.2.10
==== text
